  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Replacement of lost livelihoods assets for most affected households following 2011 floods (CB)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Exceptionally heavy monsoon rain from late July to August 2012 affected or damaged crops, fish/shrimp/crab ponds, other household assets and income generation activities. Approximately 4,277 households of the &#x2018;Improved Food and Livelihood Security&#x2019; (IFLS) programme beneficiaries in Bagerhat district, Bangladesh were affected. 

This grant will support Caritas Bangladesh in responding to the needs of the IFLS beneficiaries who were most affected by the heavy rain/floods/water logging (households that lost their livelihoods assets and households that are severely vulnerable owing to the floods), taking into account the recommendations from the mid-term review. 

CAFOD is also supporting &#xa3;50,000 for cash for work activities of Caritas Bangladesh, for 2,000 households x 10-15 man days x 500 taka (ref: Ban147: earmarked approximately &#xa3;35,000 to the cash for work component and the remainder un-earmarked for general operating costs).</narrative>
  </description>
